    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11664" root="خوأ" body-key="x">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَآءٌ</span></b>  <i>The name of the letter</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خ</span>, q. v.; as also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَا</span>: [it is called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَا</span> in a case of pause, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَآءٌ</span>
when made a noun:] it is fem. and masc.: [its
dim. is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَيَيَّةٌ</span>, meaning <i>a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خ</span> <i>written small, or indistinct:</i> (see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حَآءٌ</span> in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حوأ</span>:)] and its pl. is
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْوَآءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْيَآءٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خَاآتٌ</span>. (TA in <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">باب الالف</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الليّنة</span>.)

